# SPEC-CODEX-HOME-BACKSLASH-001 / card t571 — pre-M2 SKIP baseline

Purpose: AC-CHB-006 states an exact-equality regression criterion. "newly SKIP 0" is a delta, and a
delta cannot be decided without a pinned pre-change number. This file IS that number, measured on the
unmodified tree before M2's reordering is applied.

MEASURED_ON_HEAD=ee194493ff14bce2cf30ef790304426d53235595
MEASURED_ON_HEAD_SHORT=ee194493f
BRANCH=WT-codex-home-backslash
WORKTREE=.claude/worktrees/t571
TREE_STATE=pre-M2 — no production Go source touched by this card at measurement time
MEASURED_AT_UTC=2026-09-08T05:00:45Z
COMMAND=go test ./internal/cli/... -count=1 -timeout 600s -v
EXIT=0
SKIP_COUNT=30
SKIP_COUNT_EXPR=grep -c '^ *--- SKIP: ' <verbose-output>

Note on the counting expression: `--- SKIP:` lines are indented under their parent in `-v` output, so
the leading `^ *` is load-bearing — an anchored `^--- SKIP:` matches nothing and would report a
vacuous 0. Subtests are counted individually (four of the 30 below are subtests — measured `grep '^--- SKIP: ' <this file> | grep -c '/'` = 4), which is the
same granularity the post-M2 run must use for the equality to mean anything.

