Caveat on portability of this number: several of the 30 skip on an environment predicate (live-backend
tests, TTY probes, cross-compile helpers, exec-helper re-entry). The count is therefore pinned to THIS
host and THIS environment, not to the commit alone. The post-M2 comparison run must be made in the
same session/environment for the equality to be attributable; a run under a different environment that
differs from 30 is an environment delta, not a regression, and must be re-measured rather than reported.
